From 06978a4839fe2aff5a10c9b492836c25fc22a614 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 18:20:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Make pick-4 actually happen, Hoenn singles, in-game clause
 truth

Field report on 1.5.0: the rules screen showed entries=4 but battles ran
6v6. Disassembly found the reason: the ruleset's ENTRY MODE u16 (+0x1C) --
the effective-entries getter returns 6 whenever it is nonzero and only
honors the entries count when it is 0, while the rules screen prints the
entries count either way. The stock preset ships entry mode 1; the pin now
zeroes it (word 7), which activates the game's own bring-6-pick-N flow with
the full enforcement chain (getter, entry validator, per-participant init,
GBA reply handler, marshaller -- all traced).

Corrections and decodes riding along:
- Hoenn shapes battle SINGLE (community canon; the first implementation
  wrongly assumed doubles). The battle-type global is now emitted per
  format: 1 for Orre shapes, 0 for Hoenn.
- The clause bytes were decoded: Species, Item, Sleep, Freeze and both
  Self-KO halves are ON in the pinned stock tournament bytes -- the game
  itself enforces them. Every "honor rules" line of UI copy was wrong and
  now says so.
- Soul Dew cannot be banned in-game for custom rule slots (the bannable-
  item table has no entry for item 191; the game's hardcoded check lives
  only in the default-rules path custom slots bypass) -- the app-side
  paste/host/submission gates remain the Soul Dew enforcement, by
  structural necessity. Documented at the preset words.
- The team preview's default GC-protagonist busts (the class-0 widget
  pair) are now hidden for EVERY format session, not only for
  portrait-less picks: a format pin means GBA-vs-GBA, where that default
  head is always the wrong one. An all-default format session now still
  builds a block (guard line + bust zeroes) instead of no-oping.
